Carafe Lab: a software-window present (drisw, as on Xvfb) no longer waits for the GPU to go idle. It mapped the back
buffer for reading, which flushed and waited for all queued work, then copied it to the X image, so Eden's GPU thread
stopped for the whole frame on every present and the GPU got no new work meanwhile. Now each present queues a copy of
the back buffer into one of two staging buffers and flushes without waiting, then waits for the copy queued by the
previous present, which has normally finished, and sends that one: the window shows the frame before. The first
present after a size change maps the back buffer as before.
MIT, as the files it changes.

